sel, Switzerland."}]}},{"fullName":"Graff-Meyer A","lastName":"Graff-Meyer","firstName":"Alexandra","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Facility for Advanced Imaging and Microscopy, Friedrich Miescher Institute for Biomedical Research, 4056 Basel, Switzerland."}]}},{"fullName":"Patino-Alvarez CP","lastName":"Patino-Alvarez","firstName":"Claudia P","initials":"CP","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Molecular and Clinical Ophthalmology Basel, 4031 Basel, Switzerland."}]}},{"fullName":"Khani MH","lastName":"Khani","firstName":"Mohammad Hossein","initials":"MH","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Molecular and Clinical Ophthalmology Basel, 4031 Basel, Switzerland."}]}},{"fullName":"Jüttner J","lastName":"Jüttner","firstName":"Josephine","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Molecular and Clinical Ophthalmology Basel, 4031 Basel, Switzerland."}]}},{"fullName":"Roska B","lastName":"Roska","firstName":"Botond","initials":"B","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institute of Molecular and Clinical Ophthalmology Basel, 4031 Basel, Switzerland; Department of Ophthalmology, University of Basel, 4031 Basel, Switzerland. Electronic address: CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0973-9763"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-8050-4020"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"22","volume":"112","journalIssueId":3858309,"dateOfPublication":"2024 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":2024,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Neuron","title":"Neuron","essn":"1097-4199","issn":"0896-6273","isoabbreviation":"Neuron","nlmid":"8809320"},"printPublicationDate":"2024-11-01"},"pubYear":"2024","pageInfo":"3715-3733.e9","abstractText":"Feedback at the photoreceptor synapse is the first neuronal circuit computation in vision, which influences downstream activity patterns within the visual system. Yet, the identity of the feedback signal and the mechanism of synaptic transmission are still not well understood. Here, we combined perturbations of cell-type-specific genes of mouse horizontal cells with two-photon imaging of the result of light-induced feedback in cones and showed that the electrogenic bicarbonate transporter Slc4a5, but not the electroneutral bicarbonate transporter Slc4a3, both expressed specifically in horizontal cells, is necessary for horizontal cell-to-cone feedback. Pharmacological blockage of bicarbonate transporters and buffering pH also abolished the feedback but blocking sodium-proton exchangers and GABA receptors did not. Our work suggests an unconventional mechanism of feedback at the first visual synapse: changes in horizontal cell voltage modulate bicarbonate transport to the cell, via Slc4a5, which leads to the modulation of feedback to cones.","affiliation":"Institute of Molecular and Clinical Ophthalmology Basel, 4031 Basel, Switzerland.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Swiss National Science Foundation","acronym":"SNSF_","grantId":"CRSII3_141801","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Swiss National Science Foundation","grantId":"141801","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Louis-Jeantet Foundation","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Swiss National Science Foundation","grantId":"212186","orderIn":0},{"agency":"European Research Council","acronym":"ERC_","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Swiss National Science Foundation","acronym":"SNSF_","grantId":"310030_212186","orderIn":0},{"agency":"European Research Council","grantId":"883781","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Swiss National Science Foundation","grantId":"310030","orderIn":0},{"agency":"European Research Council","acronym":"ERC_","